<rml>
<head>
	<title>Menu</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="menu.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="game.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="menu">
	<div id="top">
		<div id="banner" data-if="banner_on">{{banner}}</div>
		<div id="welcome" data-if="welcome_on && !open">
			<div data-rml="welcome"></div>
			<div class="foot">
				<label><input type="checkbox" data-checked="welcome_remember"/>Remember</label>
				<button data-event-click="welcome_close">Close</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div id="panel" data-if="open">
		<button id="resume" data-if="booted" data-event-click="close"><span class="cap">{{menu_key}}</span>Resume</button>
		<div id="head">
			<h1>{{title}}</h1>
			<div id="nav">
				<button data-class-current="page == 'about'" data-event-click="show_page('about')">About</button>
				<button data-class-current="page == 'disks'" data-event-click="show_page('disks')">Disks</button>
				<button data-if="hacks.size > 0" data-class-current="page == 'hacks'" data-event-click="show_page('hacks')">Hacks</button>
				<button data-if="controls" data-class-current="page == 'controls'" data-event-click="show_page('controls')">Controls</button>
				<button data-class-current="page == 'settings'" data-event-click="show_page('settings')">Settings</button>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div id="page">
			<div data-if="page == 'about'">
				<p class="lead">Your own copy of {{title}}, running natively on this computer.</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<button class="primary" data-event-click="open_disk">Open Disk…</button>
					<button data-if="booted" data-event-click="reset">Reset</button>
					<button data-event-click="quit">Quit</button>
				</div>
				<div class="actions" data-if="desktop_offered">
					<button data-if="!desktop_installed" data-event-click="desktop('add')">Add to applications menu</button>
					<button data-if="desktop_installed" data-event-click="desktop('remove')">Remove from applications menu</button>
					<p class="hint" data-if="desktop_note != ''">{{desktop_note}}</p>
				</div>
				<p data-if="!booted">To start, choose your disk images with Open Disk…, or drop them on this window. ADF, ADZ, GZ and ZIP files are accepted, and one ZIP may hold every disk. The Disks page shows which disks are still missing.</p>
				<div class="about" data-rml="about"></div>
				<h2>AmigaRecomp</h2>
				<p>AmigaRecomp runs Amiga games natively, one program per game. The game's code runs on the Musashi 68000 interpreter plus a recreated Amiga chipset (copper, bitplanes, sprites, blitter, CIAs and Paula audio) written by Claude AI. Kickstart 1.3 is replaced by C code, so no ROM is needed.</p>
				<p>The project contains <span class="underline">no game code and no game data</span>. Some optional hacks slightly improve the experience.</p>
				<h2>Keys</h2>
				<div class="key"><span class="label">{{menu_key}}</span><span class="state">this menu; {{menu_key}} or Esc closes it once the game runs</span></div>
				<div class="key" data-if="state_keys"><span class="label">F5 / F9</span><span class="state">quick save / quick load</span></div>
				<div class="key"><span class="label">F12</span><span class="state">screenshot of the game screen</span></div>
				<div class="key"><span class="label">Alt+Enter</span><span class="state">fullscreen on / off</span></div>
				<div class="key" data-if="controls"><span class="label">bound keys</span><span class="state">the joystick in port 2; see the Controls page</span></div>
				<div class="key" data-if="controls"><span class="label">a controller</span><span class="state">the joystick in port 2 too: left stick or D-pad, buttons as on the Controls page</span></div>
				<div class="key" data-if="two_joysticks"><span class="label">2nd controller</span><span class="state">player 2's joystick, in port 1</span></div>
			</div>
			<div data-if="page == 'disks'">
				<h2>Drives</h2>
				<div class="drive" data-for="d, n : drives">
					<span class="label">{{d.name}}</span>
					<span class="state" data-if="!booted">{{d.disk}}</span>
					<span class="toggle" data-if="booted"><span data-for="c : drive_choices"><button data-class-chosen="c.role == d.role" data-event-click="insert(n, c.role)">{{c.label}}</button></span></span>
				</div>
				<p class="hint" data-if="!booted">The game starts with these disks in its drives. Once it runs, choose the disk in each drive here.</p>
				<h2>Game disks</h2>
				<div class="disk" data-for="disk, i : disks">
					<span class="label">{{disk.label}}</span>
					<span class="state">{{disk.state}}</span>
					<span class="source">{{disk.source}}</span>
					<button data-if="disk.writable" data-event-click="import_disk(i)">Load save disk…</button>
					<p class="hint" data-if="disk.writable">Copies the ADF you choose into this file; your file is not changed.</p>
				</div>
				<p data-if="!booted">Provide the missing disks using Open Disk…, by dropping files on this window, or as paths on the command line. ADF, ADZ, GZ and ZIP are accepted.</p>
				<div data-if="!booted" class="actions"><button class="primary" data-event-click="open_disk">Open Disk…</button></div>
				<p class="message" data-for="m : messages">{{m}}</p>
				<h2>Save states</h2>
				<p data-if="!booted">Save states can be used once the game has started.</p>
				<div class="actions" data-if="booted">
					<button data-event-click="state_save">Quick save</button>
					<button data-event-click="state_load">Quick load</button>
					<button data-event-click="state_save_as">Save to…</button>
					<button data-event-click="state_load_from">Load from…</button>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div data-if="page == 'hacks'">
				<p>Hacks change small behaviours of the game: original keeps the game's own behaviour, modern changes it. A change applies immediately and is remembered.</p>
				<div class="option" data-for="h, i : hacks" data-class-mismatch="h.status == 'mismatch'">
					<span class="name">{{h.label}}</span>
					<span class="toggle" data-if="h.type == 'bool'"><button data-class-chosen="h.value == 0" data-event-click="choose('hack', i, 0)">original</button><button data-class-chosen="h.value == 1" data-event-click="choose('hack', i, 1)">modern</button></span>
					<span data-if="h.type == 'choice'"><button data-for="c, j : h.choices" data-class-chosen="j == h.value" data-event-click="choose('hack', i, j)">{{c}}</button></span>
					<p class="hint">{{h.hint}}</p>
					<p class="hint" data-if="h.status == 'mismatch'">not compatible with this disk image</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div data-if="page == 'controls'">
				<p>Rebind Amiga's joystick in port 2 to your keyboard keys and controller buttons.</p>
				<div class="command" data-for="c, i : commands">
					<span class="label">{{c.label}}</span>
					<span class="keys">
						<button class="keycap" data-for="k : c.keys" data-event-click="unbind_key(k.input)">{{k.name}}<span class="remove">×</span></button>
						<button data-if="binding != i" data-event-click="bind_key(i)">Add key…</button>
						<span class="waiting" data-if="binding == i">Press a key or a controller button (Esc cancels)</span>
					</span>
				</div>
				<p class="hint">Click a key or button to unbind it. {{menu_key}}, <span data-if="state_keys">F5, F9, </span>F12 and Esc stay with this program and cannot be bound.</p>
				<p class="hint">A game controller works the joystick too, alongside these keys: the left stick or the D-pad steers, and its buttons do what they are bound to here, Pad A, B, X and Y by their places on an Xbox controller (any button fires on a plain joystick). Button 2 is the second button of a two-button joystick, which most games ignore.<span data-if="two_joysticks"> A second controller is player 2's joystick, in port 1.</span></p>
				<div class="actions"><button data-event-click="bind_defaults">Restore defaults</button></div>
			</div>
			<div data-if="page == 'settings'">
				<div class="option" data-for="s, i : settings">
					<span class="name">{{s.label}}</span>
					<span class="toggle" data-if="s.type == 'bool'"><button data-class-chosen="s.value == 0" data-event-click="choose('setting', i, 0)">off</button><button data-class-chosen="s.value == 1" data-event-click="choose('setting', i, 1)">on</button></span>
					<span class="toggle" data-if="s.type == 'choice'"><button data-for="c, j : s.choices" data-class-chosen="j == s.value" data-event-click="choose('setting', i, j)">{{c}}</button></span>
					<p class="hint">{{s.hint}}</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div id="notes"><div data-for="n : notes"><div class="note" data-class-error="n.error" data-style-opacity="n.opacity">{{n.text}}</div></div></div>
	<div id="disk_light" data-if="disk_light"><img src="floppy.png"/></div>
</body>
</rml>
